Handle O_ADDTABLE in ipfw_chk() and wire init/destroy lifecycle in ip_fw2.c.

The action is non-terminal (like O_COUNT): enqueues the address addition
asynchronously then continues rule evaluation. IPFW_INC_RULE_COUNTER is
called so hit/byte counts are updated correctly.

ipfw_addtable_init() is called after ipfw_init_tables() so the table
subsystem is ready. ipfw_addtable_destroy() is called before
ipfw_destroy_tables() to drain in-flight tasks first.
